schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: DAO Voting Mechanisms
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    The family of mechanisms DAOs use to turn proposals into decisions —
    ranging from simple token-weighted quorum voting to quadratic voting,
    time-weighted conviction voting, prediction-market-based holographic
    consensus, small-group multi-sig approval, and gasless off-chain
    signature voting.
  source_traditions:
    - traditional deliberative-assembly quorum rules (the article's own "general assembly" analogy)
    - Gitcoin's quadratic funding mechanism design
    - Giveth's conviction voting implementation
    - prediction-market mechanism design (holographic consensus)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Used as a comparison menu for DAO operators, explicitly concluding that
    most mature DAOs layer multiple mechanisms rather than picking one.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - quorum voting as practiced in non-blockchain cooperative boards and community associations (the article notes Somaliland/East-Africa cooperative boards face the same low-active-participation dynamic, without naming a specific case or source)
  important_distinctions:
    - on-chain quorum/token voting (simple, plutocratic) vs quadratic voting (cost rises with the square of votes cast, dampening wealth dominance)
    - conviction voting (time-weighted, cannot be swung last-minute) vs holographic consensus (prediction-market-based proposal triage)
    - full-community voting vs multi-sig (small trusted group, fast but centralized)
  tensions:
    - decentralization ideal vs the practical need for fast multi-sig decisions on routine/emergency matters
    - manipulation-resistance (conviction voting, quadratic voting) vs added complexity and slower decisions
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Presenting these six mechanisms as a tidy toolkit risks understating
    that each embeds different values about whose voice counts more (wealth,
    time-commitment, prediction-market savvy, or trusted-group membership) —
    the article does gesture at this ("depends on your community's values")
    but doesn't work through any single mechanism's failure modes in depth.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/voting-mechanisms.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  source_lineage: voting-mechanisms.md
